  "solution": {
    "text": "Lithium aluminium hydride can be prepared by the reaction of dimer of aluminium trichloride and lithium hydride by the below reaction with a high yield:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>LiH</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>LiAlH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>LiCl</mi></math><br />Lithium aluminium hydride is extensively used for reduction of organic compounds.",
